/*!

*\page goto Goto
*
* A goto statement provides an unconditional jump from the 'goto' to a labeled statement or start of a script program. It must be in the same function<BR>
* Goto might be a better choice than while loop or for loop since there are less calculations in the script engine. This can increase speed and performance of the script program.
*<span style='color:blue'><em><H4> Syntax: </H4></em></span>
*<B> goto LABEL </B>
*Note:
*		Label: must be defined for goto statment works. If you jump to an undefined label, script program execution will fails. 
* <span style='color:blue'><em><B> <br>
Example:
</B> </em> </span><br>
*   goto exitPoint;	  						&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem goto exit </span><br>
*   print "Unexecuted instruction\n";<br>
*		....<br>
* 	:exitPoint:    						    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem Label definition </span><br>
*	print "I am going out!!\n";		&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem send to serial "I am going out!!" </span><br>
*
*/
